y incomplete (2-5 of 7 days per property, confirmed via identical retry on two properties -- not the query-merge bug). Walked back one more week to Oct 16-22: reconfirmed fully complete (7/7 days, all 13 GBP-connected properties) and verified identical to the already-published figures (spot-checked Lakeside/Lakeview exactly). GBP_CURRENT stays at Oct 16-22, 2026 for a 3rd consecutive run -- not a stall, this window is simply stable and mature now. GBP_PRIOR re-pulled fresh for Oct 9-15, 2026 (confirmed complete, 7/7 days): reach_search/reach_maps/website_clicks/directions_clicks all matched the previously-derived baseline exactly (5314/1378/577/626), but phone_clicks came back 280 this run -- reverting from last run's 277 back to the original 280. This specific field continues to show small +/-3 unit intraday/multi-day volatility on this now-3-week-old window even though every other field has fully stabilized; not treating it as an error, just re-using whatever the live pull shows each time. Because GBP_CURRENT itself is unchanged (still Oct 16-22 vs Oct 9-15), every GMB tile's current value is identical to last week; only phone_clicks' delta shifts from -37 back to -40 to reflect the revised prior-week baseline. posts_published unchanged (GBP_CURRENT=8, GBP_PRIOR=6) -- not re-verified via getScheduledPosts a third time since the window itself didn't change and this field isn't subject to backfill lag. Views KPI, views_by_channel, and every property's views_channels/top_channel recomputed this run using the unchanged GBP Reach proxy; engagement KPI and the Google Business engagement_by_channel entry use the unchanged GBP clicks total (1,502).\n\nURL Tracking: no new GA4 export this week -- carried forward unchanged from last week's real Oct 22-29 reading (applied 2026-10-30), delta zeroed. GMB URL Tracking is still held pending a window match: gbp_window_label is still \"Oct 16 - 22, 2026\", so the real Oct 22-29 GMB numbers documented in last week's generated_note 